SWEET AOC pre-load probe (patch 0374, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step A4), boot-arg sweetaoc=1. READS ONLY. Round 3 after runs
o6-a4-aoc (hang before USB) and o6-a4-aoc2 (system stall right after "aoc: reading acpm"): the APM SRAM / ACPM channel 13 block is
dropped. Order: the PMU AOC power-domain status 0x17461884 bit 0 (flexpmu_cal_local_gs101.h:3-20), the GSA mailbox 0x17C90000
status/shared registers, then aoc_req 0x175D0000 and the AOC SysMMU 0x1A090000 only when that bit is 1, else "skipped: pd off".
The AOC S2MPU 0x1A0B0000 is never read. The probe runs in its own thread once the USB log has sent a datagram (counter
sweet_usblog_sent in sweet_usb.c, bounded 300 s), prints "SWEET AOC PRE: aoc: reading <block>" 500 ms before each block and that
block's values right after its reads. Started from the top of sweet_trusty_init (patch 0372), the same hook point as sweetamp.
Cites in bsd/dev/sweet_aoc.h (host test shim/aoc_pre_host_test.c). Last line "SWEET AOC PRE: verdict PASS|FAIL reads=N pd=on|off".
Without the boot-arg nothing changes.

